Release-preset Linux binaries link libmad 0.15.1b statically. libmad is copyright
Robert Leslie and is distributed under the GNU GPL. The release includes a
companion source archive containing the corresponding Debian libmad source
package (0.15.1b-11, used by the 0.15.1b-11+b1 development package).

GLib, libcurl, libogg, libvorbis and the C runtime are dynamically linked system
dependencies; their notices and source packages are provided by their projects
and operating-system packages. These libraries are not bundled in the binary
tarball.

The Debian package instead links the system libmad dynamically and declares
its runtime dependency through Debian's shared-library dependency metadata.
